<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/assinie"><span class="enc-name">Assinie</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Assinie is a coastal town in south-eastern Ivory Coast, on the sandbar between the Aby lagoon and the Gulf of Guinea.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/assisi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/assisi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Assisi</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Assisi is a hill town in Umbria, central Italy, the birthplace of Saint Francis and Saint Clare.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/assizes-of-antioch"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/assizes-of-antioch.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Assizes of Antioch</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Assizes of Antioch were the law code of the crusader Principality of Antioch, regulating feudal relations, the courts and the rights of burgesses.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/assizes-of-ariano"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/assizes-of-ariano.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Assizes of Ariano</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Assizes of Ariano are a collection of laws issued by Roger II of Sicily, traditionally at an assembly in Ariano in 1140.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/assizes-of-jerusalem"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/assizes-of-jerusalem.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Assizes of Jerusalem</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Assizes of Jerusalem are a collection of medieval legal treatises setting out the laws and customs of the crusader Kingdom of Jerusalem and the Kingdom of Cyprus.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/assizes-of-romania"><span class="enc-name">Assizes of Romania</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Assizes of Romania is a code of feudal law compiled in the Principality of Achaea in the first half of the 14th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/associates-of-the-swiss-confederacy"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/associates-of-the-swiss-confederacy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Associates of the Swiss Confederacy</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">The Associates of the Swiss Confederacy, in German zugewandte Orte, were territories allied to the Old Swiss Confederacy without being full member cantons.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/association-of-southeast-asian-nations"><span class="enc-name">Association of Southeast Asian Nations</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) is a regional organisation founded in Bangkok in August 1967 by Indonesia, Malaysia, the Philippines, Singapore and…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/assur"><span class="enc-name">Assur</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Assur was an ancient city on the Tigris in northern Iraq and the religious and original political capital of Assyria, named after its chief god.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/assur-fernandez"><span class="enc-name">Assur Fernández</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Assur Fernández was a Castilian noble whom Ramiro II of León made count of Monzón, near Palencia, around 943.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/assynt"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/assynt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Assynt</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Assynt is a mountainous district on the west coast of Sutherland in the north-west Highlands of Scotland, centred on the village of Lochinver.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-conquest-of-babylon-c-1225-bce"><span class="enc-name">Assyrian conquest of Babylon (c. 1225 BCE)</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · c. 1225 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Assyrian conquest of Babylon around c. 1225 BCE was the capture of the city by the Middle Assyrian king Tukulti-Ninurta I.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-conquest-of-egypt"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/assyrian-conquest-of-egypt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Assyrian conquest of Egypt</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 671 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Assyrian conquest of Egypt was the invasion of Egypt by the Assyrian king Esarhaddon, who captured Memphis in 671 BCE and drove out the Kushite pharaoh Taharqa.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-destruction-of-susa"><span class="enc-name">Assyrian destruction of Susa</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 646 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Assyrian destruction of Susa was the sack of the Elamite capital by the army of Ashurbanipal in 646 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Assyrian Empire</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Assyrian Empire was a Mesopotamian state centred on Assur and Nineveh on the upper Tigris.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/asta-gudbrandsdatter"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/asta-gudbrandsdatter.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Åsta Gudbrandsdatter</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Åsta Gudbrandsdatter was a Norwegian noblewoman of the late 10th and early 11th centuries, according to the sagas.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/astana"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/astana.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Astana</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Astana is the capital of Kazakhstan, on the Ishim River in the north of the country.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/astana-cemetery"><span class="enc-name">Astana Cemetery</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Astana Cemetery is an ancient burial ground near the ruins of Gaochang, east of Turpan in Xinjiang, China.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/astana-gede"><span class="enc-name">Astana Gede</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Astana Gede is a sacred site at Kawali in Ciamis Regency, West Java, Indonesia, associated with the Sundanese kingdom of Galuh.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/astara"><span class="enc-name">Astara</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Astara is a town on the Caspian coast divided by the Astara river between Azerbaijan and Iran, the two halves forming separate towns.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/astarte"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/astarte.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Astarte</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Astarte was a major goddess of the ancient Levant, worshipped by Phoenicians, Canaanites and others as a deity of love, fertility and war.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aster-revolution"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/aster-revolution.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Aster Revolution</span><span class="enc-type">Revolution · 1918</span><span class="enc-snip">The Aster Revolution was the uprising in Budapest of 28-31 October 1918, as Austria-Hungary collapsed at the end of the First World War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/astorga"><span class="enc-name">Astorga</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Astorga is a town in the province of León in north-western Spain.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/astorre-iii-manfredi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/astorre-iii-manfredi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Astorre III Manfredi</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Astorre III Manfredi was the last Manfredi lord of Faenza in Romagna.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/astrakhan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/astrakhan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Astrakhan</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Astrakhan is a city on the Volga delta near the Caspian Sea, in southern Russia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/astrakhan-khanate"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/astrakhan-khanate.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Astrakhan Khanate</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Astrakhan Khanate was a Tatar state on the lower Volga, centred on the city of Astrakhan, that emerged from the break-up of the Golden Horde in the fifteenth century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/asturia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/asturia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Asturia</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Asturia was the Roman name for the lands of the Astures in north-western Hispania, covering modern Asturias, the province of León and neighbouring areas.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/asturias"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/asturias.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Asturias</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Asturias is an autonomous community and historic region on the Bay of Biscay coast of northern Spain, separated from the Meseta by the Cantabrian Mountains.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/asturica-augusta"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/asturica-augusta.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Asturica Augusta</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Asturica Augusta was the Roman town on the site of Astorga in north-western Spain, founded after Augustus' Cantabrian Wars in the land of the Astures.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/astyages"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/astyages.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Astyages</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Astyages was the last king of the Median Empire in the sixth century BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/asuka-dera"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/asuka-dera.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Asuka-dera</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Asuka-dera is a Buddhist temple in Asuka, Nara Prefecture, and one of the oldest in Japan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/asuncion"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/asuncion.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Asunción</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Asunción is the capital and largest city of Paraguay, on the east bank of the Paraguay river.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/aswan-high-dam"><span class="enc-name">Aswan High Dam</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Aswan High Dam is a rock-fill dam across the Nile at Aswan in southern Egypt, built between 1960 and 1970 with Soviet finance and engineering after the United…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/asyut"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/asyut.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Asyut</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Asyut is a city on the Nile in Upper Egypt.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/at-turaif"><span class="enc-name">At-Turaif</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">At-Turaif is the historic citadel district of Diriyah, near Riyadh, which served as the seat of the first Saudi state in the 18th and early 19th centuries.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/atahualpa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/atahualpa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Atahualpa</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Atahualpa was the last Sapa Inca of the Inca Empire before the Spanish conquest.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/atai"><span class="enc-name">Ataï</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ataï was a Kanak high chief from the region of La Foa in New Caledonia who led the great